  "index": 1,
  "response": "The two passages describe exploitative labor systems in different parts of the world:\n\n**Passage 1 (Huanacavelica and Potos\u00ed, Peru):**  Focuses on the *mita* system, where Indians were forced to work in silver mines. Conditions were harsh, with dangerous working environments, low pay, and corrupt overseers. The passage highlights the misery inflicted on indigenous people by this system.\n\n**Passage 2 (Yakut and Tungus natives in Siberia):**  Describes the *yasak* tribute system imposed by Russian rulers. Natives were forced to pay taxes in furs or cash. Overhunting due to the yasak led to depleted animal populations, further impoverishing the natives.  The passage shows how this system devastated local economies and traditions.\n\n\nBoth passages expose the brutal consequences of colonial exploitation, highlighting the suffering and loss inflicted on indigenous people through forced labor and oppressive tribute systems. \n",
